    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d656">

                <pb facs="0811" n="717" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg717"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Williams to Mr. Olney.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Habana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-05-08"><hi rendition="#italic">May 8,
                        1896</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>I have seen prisoners this morning. Laborde, captain <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Competitor</hi>, tells me was born New Orleans and formerly was deputy
                    sheriff Tampa. Was going Lemon City with twenty four passengers when they seized
                    the vessel by force, putting pistol to his breast, and took command. Off Cape
                    Sable took on board twenty-three men more. William Gildea, mate, born Liverpool,
                    England; Ona Milton, born Kansas.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
